Two Loom AIE2P array fixes for leaf-synchronized channels (yah gen_npu_gemm ghelp: a helper core decodes a K row and
sends its records to the head through a leaf-synced neighbor-memory ring):
- A leaf-synchronized port's ring address never changes across firings (the leaf walks the slots itself), but the
  resident wrapper carried it as firing-loop state like any other port's. Every such address then held a pointer
  register through the whole leaf; a leaf with a few of them plus its own pointers ran out (pointer peak 10 / 8). The
  address is now rematerialized where the leaf imports the resource and is no longer loop state.
- A leaf-synced neighbor-memory ring was placed like a DMA ring, slot by slot round-robin over the banks (slot 1 at
  +16384), while the leaf steps its slots by the record length. It is now one contiguous allocation, as leaf-synced
  compute rings already are. Images without leaf-synced neighbor channels are unchanged in layout.
